      ],
      "description": "Ownership by trust rather than proprietor shapes this newsroom's behaviour in ways monitors learn to anticipate: investigations run long, follow-ups arrive in waves, and a story a client hopes has passed can resurface weeks later with new documents. Its feed provision is among the most generous of any British national, covering desks most rivals stopped syndicating years ago. For reputation work the Media desk deserves particular attention, as it is where coverage about coverage tends to start. The open-access model also means every link in a morning brief resolves for every reader, which matters more than it sounds."
    },
    {
