      ],
      "description": "Reach is the whole argument here. A story that makes the broadcaster's front page reaches an audience an order of magnitude beyond any national newspaper, so crisis teams treat its pickup as the threshold between a trade story and a public one. Less obvious to newcomers is how conservative the desk feeds are: syndicated output trails the website's live pages by several minutes during breaking news, which is worth knowing before promising anyone real-time alerts. Regional output is thinner in the feeds than on air, a gap Inkline flags rather than papers over."
    },
    {
