      ],
      "description": "A weekly rhythm makes this title easy to monitor badly. The print edition lands Thursday evening London time, and that is when a fortnight of quiet can turn into the definitive framing of an issue, unsigned and therefore speaking with the full weight of the institution. Bylines are absent by policy, which changes how a mention should be escalated: there is no correspondent relationship to manage, only an editorial line. Daily digital pieces between editions have grown steadily and now justify continuous monitoring rather than a Thursday check."
    },
