      ],
      "description": "For a London comms team the practical question is timing, and the answer is awkward: the heaviest publishing window opens as the UK working day ends, so a Journal story about a European client often breaks into an unstaffed evening. Building it into an automated evening brief solves what a manual check cannot. Heard on the Street occupies roughly the position Lex does at its London rival, brief and market-moving, and Opinion operates with a noticeably freer hand than the news desks. Feed coverage is stable but narrower than the site's full section map."
    },
