      ],
      "description": "Anyone monitoring a DAX-listed client learns quickly that the German business conversation runs through Düsseldorf, not Frankfurt. Company coverage here regularly carries supervisory-board detail the international press picks up a day later, and often only partially. The weekday publishing pattern is pronounced, with output thinning sharply after Friday afternoon, so a weekend gap in mentions is normal rather than a monitoring fault. Inkline pairs it with on-device summarisation, which turns German-language desk output into something an English-speaking team can actually triage at speed."
    },
