      "description": "The afternoon matters here in a way that trips up monitors calibrated to London or New York rhythms. This paper's heritage as an evening title survives in its publishing curve, which peaks after lunch Paris time, so a morning-only sweep of French coverage will consistently miss its lead stories. An English-language edition now runs in parallel and is worth adding for teams without French, though it carries a subset of the desks. Économie coverage of French-listed companies tends toward the analytical rather than the incremental, which makes it better for context than for alerts."
    },
